(4) The depth of the well;
(5) The length of the casing to be used in connection with the well;
(6) The purpose for which the water from the well is to be used;
(7) The maximum amount of water to be obtained from the well;
(8) The aquifer from which the water is to be obtained;
(9) Safeguards to be installed which would prohibit the contamination of the aquifer from surface waters;
(10) An opinion from a geologist, expert in the field, that the drilling and the proposed use of the well will not interfere with the public water supply of the city, tend to contaminate the water supply of the city or add dissolved iron to the water supply of the city.
(Code 1981, § 15-65; Code 1992, § 5-86)

